cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "UA-OSM: Uncertainty-Aware Object-Shaped Merging to Reduce Object Loss in 360° Surround-View Stitching"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Joshi
    given-names: Rohit
    affiliation: "EIMT, Switzerland"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4201-7862"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-27"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/GITHUB_USER/UA-OSM"
abstract: >-
  Simulation code, validation notebook and result data for UA-OSM, a merging method for
  four-camera surround-view systems that assigns each object's complete ground-projected
  footprint to one camera that detects it, dilates it by tracker covariance, resolves
  conflicts by joint camera assignment and escalates to a driver warning when an object
  cannot be shown whole.
keywords:
  - surround view
  - image stitching
  - fisheye camera
  - vulnerable road users
  - parallax
  - ADAS
  - SOTIF
